    "paragraph": "\"Estimating Pedestrian Volumes from GIS-Derived Built-Environment Features\" developed a machine learning pipeline to predict peak pedestrian volumes at urban intersections in Portland, Oregon, using open GIS data. \"Global maps of travel time to emergency and tertiary hospitals\" mapped global drive-time access to over 217,000 hospitals using OpenStreetMap routing and population data. \"Linking COPD Prevalence with Income Distribution\" developed a geographically weighted penalized compositional regression model to analyze income distribution data as compositional covariates while detecting regional clusters with shared regression effects.",
